Key nvcc's --keep directory off the output object

The wrapper passes --keep, which writes intermediates named after the source
stem into the working directory. Under Bazel that is the one execroot every
action shares, so the PIC and non-PIC compiles of a source write the same
files, and ptxas reads a .ptx the other nvcc is still writing. The failure is
a ptxas parsing error at a different arch and line each run. Each added
-gencode makes it more likely.
